en:
The charged weak current is purely left-chiral. The lecture first names the $Z$, then corrects the statement to the $W^\pm$: $Z$ couplings are chiral and unequal, but not simply absent for every right-chiral fermion. The clean statement is $\mathcal L_{\mathrm{cc}}
  =
  -\frac{g}{\sqrt2}
  \left(\bar u_L\gamma^\mu d_L
